<title>SWEDEN: Swedish May unemployment falls to 7.8 percent.</title>
<headline>Swedish May unemployment falls to 7.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unemployment in Sweden fell to 7.8 percent in May from 8.3 percent in April, Statistics Sweden said on Friday.  </p>
<p> SWEDISH UNEMPLOYMENT	 May 97	April 97   May 96</p>
<p> Percent of workforce	 7.8	   8.3	  7.1</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	 329,000     350,000    300,000</p>
<p>Note - A Reuters poll of economists showed the market had expected an unemployment rate of 7.9 percent in May. Sweden's Labour Market Board Ams said on Thursday May unemployment rose to 7.6 percent from 7.5 percent in April.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
